WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Here is a sealed glass flask, heated to

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.200
about two hundred and fifty degrees Celsius and

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.400
held there, hot enough that everything inside stays

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.680
a gas.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.320
We fill it with just one gas, phosphorus

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.840
pentachloride, written P C L five, and nothing

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.040
else.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.173
This reaction is reversible.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:21.280
A P C L five molecule can split

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.480
into phosphorus trichloride, P C L three, and

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.120
chlorine, and those two can join back up

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.040
into P C L five.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.280
But right now the flask holds only P

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.280
C L five, so there is nothing yet

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.880
to run backwards.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.800
So how does a flask that starts with

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.280
only reactant end up as a mixture that

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.440
stays exactly the same?

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.280
To find out, we'll follow it from the

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.560
moment it's sealed.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:49.446
At the very beginning, the flask holds 0.20

00:00:49.607 --> 00:00:51.526
moles of P C L five in every

00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:52.486
litre.

00:00:52.647 --> 00:00:54.966
That is its concentration, and there is no

00:00:55.047 --> 00:00:57.686
P C L three or chlorine at all.

00:00:58.007 --> 00:01:00.326
In the equation, the reaction going left to

00:01:00.407 --> 00:01:03.726
right, here splitting, is the forward reaction.

00:01:04.007 --> 00:01:06.566
The one going right to left, joining, is

00:01:06.647 --> 00:01:08.046
the reverse reaction.

00:01:08.327 --> 00:01:10.326
Every P C L five molecule is a

00:01:10.407 --> 00:01:13.686
candidate to split, and some do every second,

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.446
so the forward reaction can begin straight away.

00:01:16.727 --> 00:01:19.206
On a made-up scale, where bigger means more

00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:21.926
splits each second, the forward rate starts at

00:01:22.087 --> 00:01:22.766
fifty.

00:01:23.047 --> 00:01:25.326
The reverse reaction can't start yet.

00:01:25.527 --> 00:01:27.926
To rejoin, a P C L three molecule

00:01:28.007 --> 00:01:30.406
has to meet a chlorine molecule, and neither

00:01:30.687 --> 00:01:31.046
exists.

00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:33.926
So the reverse rate is exactly zero.

00:01:35.134 --> 00:01:37.053
A little later, some of the P C

00:01:37.134 --> 00:01:38.533
L five has split.

00:01:38.814 --> 00:01:42.333
The flask now holds 0.16 moles per litre

00:01:42.414 --> 00:01:45.693
of P C L five, and 0.04 moles

00:01:45.774 --> 00:01:47.373
per litre of each product.

00:01:48.014 --> 00:01:50.333
The forward rate has dropped from fifty to

00:01:50.414 --> 00:01:51.253
forty.

00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:53.693
Each P C L five molecule has the

00:01:53.774 --> 00:01:56.573
same chance of splitting in any one second,

00:01:56.654 --> 00:01:59.213
so with fewer molecules in the flask, fewer

00:01:59.294 --> 00:02:00.133
split.

00:02:00.574 --> 00:02:02.973
Meanwhile, the reverse reaction has started.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.413
P C L three and chlorine now exist,

00:02:06.494 --> 00:02:08.893
so now and then one of each meets

00:02:08.974 --> 00:02:11.333
and joins back into P C L five.

00:02:11.614 --> 00:02:13.293
That's a reverse rate of eight.

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.733
But forward is still bigger than reverse, so

00:02:16.814 --> 00:02:18.973
more P C L five splits each second

00:02:19.054 --> 00:02:22.493
than is rebuilt, and its concentration keeps falling,

00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:23.533
but more slowly.

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:27.213
Later again, P C L five is down

00:02:27.254 --> 00:02:30.973
to 0.14 moles per litre, and each product

00:02:31.134 --> 00:02:33.413
is up to 0.06.

00:02:33.774 --> 00:02:36.573
The forward rate has slipped to thirty-five, because

00:02:36.654 --> 00:02:38.373
there is even less to split.

00:02:38.654 --> 00:02:41.533
The reverse rate has climbed to seventeen, because

00:02:41.654 --> 00:02:43.693
with more P C L three and chlorine

00:02:43.774 --> 00:02:45.933
in the same space, they find each other

00:02:46.014 --> 00:02:46.813
more often.

00:02:47.134 --> 00:02:50.093
The gap between the two rates is shrinking.

00:02:50.174 --> 00:02:52.253
While the forward rate is bigger, P C

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.413
L five is lost faster than it is

00:02:54.614 --> 00:02:57.213
made, so it is still falling, just more

00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:58.173
slowly again.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.400
Then comes the moment they are equal.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.680
At 0.12 moles per litre of P C

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.680
L five and 0.08 of each product, both

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.520
rates are thirty.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.680
Now P C L five is made as

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.320
fast as it is lost, so its concentration

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.720
stops changing.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.440
That is why the P C L five

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.880
never runs out.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.680
Both reactions are still running at thirty, and

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.200
their effects cancel.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.160
That is the dynamic equilibrium from last time.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.520
You can even see it.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.880
Chlorine is a pale yellow-green gas, while P

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.120
C L five vapour is pale and nearly

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.120
colourless, so the flask slowly turns yellow-green, then

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.240
stops getting any darker, because the chlorine concentration

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.680
has stopped changing.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.340
Here is the whole journey as graphs.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.540
First, the concentrations.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.660
P C L five falls, then flattens.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.540
P C L three and chlorine rise together,

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.540
and flatten too, because they are made in

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:57.500
equal numbers.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.660
Notice they flatten at 0.08 moles per litre,

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.100
below the P C L five at 0.12.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.620
The concentrations don't have to match.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:08.980
Now the rates.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.060
The forward rate starts high and falls.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.260
The reverse rate starts at zero and rises.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.900
Where the two lines meet, the concentrations stop

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.260
changing, and from there both rates stay level.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.340
Check the height of that flat line: it

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.500
is thirty, not zero.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.340
A common slip is to say the reaction

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.100
stops at equilibrium.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:30.860
Neither rate drops to zero.

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.146
Remember the two towns from the last video?

00:04:34.627 --> 00:04:36.986
Start with everyone in the left town.

00:04:37.187 --> 00:04:39.826
At first, all the traffic flows from left

00:04:39.907 --> 00:04:40.466
to right.

00:04:40.867 --> 00:04:43.186
With fewer people left in the left town,

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.946
less traffic leaves it each minute.

00:04:45.347 --> 00:04:47.586
And as the right town fills up, more

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:48.626
cars head back.

00:04:49.027 --> 00:04:51.586
The traffic going left builds until it matches

00:04:51.627 --> 00:04:53.746
the traffic going right, and from then on

00:04:53.987 --> 00:04:57.186
the populations stay steady, although cars still drive

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:58.186
both ways.

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:00.706
In our flask, the forward rate is the

00:05:00.787 --> 00:05:02.066
faster one at the start.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.626
If we had started with only products, it

00:05:04.707 --> 00:05:06.026
would be the other way round.

00:05:06.227 --> 00:05:08.386
So in a sealed flask at a steady

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:11.666
temperature, hold onto this line: the faster rate

00:05:11.747 --> 00:05:15.186
falls, the slower rate rises, they meet and

00:05:15.347 --> 00:05:16.146
stay level.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.366
Your turn, with a different start.

00:05:20.007 --> 00:05:22.646
A new sealed flask, the same size, at

00:05:22.727 --> 00:05:26.486
the same temperature, is filled with 0.20 moles

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:28.886
per litre of P C L three and

00:05:28.967 --> 00:05:32.566
0.20 of chlorine, and no P C L

00:05:32.647 --> 00:05:33.366
five at all.

00:05:34.007 --> 00:05:35.286
Answer three things.

00:05:35.847 --> 00:05:38.486
One: which rate is zero at the very

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:39.846
start, and why?

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:44.326
Two: as time passes, which rate falls, which

00:05:44.407 --> 00:05:47.126
rises, and what happens to the concentration of

00:05:47.207 --> 00:05:48.086
each substance?

00:05:48.727 --> 00:05:51.446
Three: once the two rates are equal, are

00:05:51.527 --> 00:05:52.886
the reactions still going?

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.446
Pause the video if you'd like more time.

00:06:30.867 --> 00:06:33.666
At the start, the forward rate is zero,

00:06:33.787 --> 00:06:35.426
because there is no P C L five

00:06:35.507 --> 00:06:36.706
yet to split.

00:06:36.867 --> 00:06:39.506
Only the reverse reaction can happen: P C

00:06:39.587 --> 00:06:42.386
L three and chlorine meet and join.

00:06:42.507 --> 00:06:44.786
So P C L five rises from zero

00:06:45.027 --> 00:06:48.306
to 0.12 moles per litre, while P C

00:06:48.387 --> 00:06:51.186
L three and chlorine fall from 0.20 to

00:06:51.347 --> 00:06:55.266
0.08, the same mixture as before.

00:06:55.507 --> 00:06:58.466
That happens because the total phosphorus and chlorine,

00:06:58.547 --> 00:07:00.706
the flask size and the temperature are the

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:01.186
same.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.306
Here is how the rates change.

00:07:03.507 --> 00:07:05.906
The reverse rate falls, because those two are

00:07:05.987 --> 00:07:08.866
being used up, and the forward rate rises,

00:07:08.987 --> 00:07:11.026
because P C L five is building up.

00:07:11.347 --> 00:07:14.146
So the aid still holds: the reverse rate

00:07:14.227 --> 00:07:16.386
was the faster one, and it fell.

00:07:16.467 --> 00:07:19.586
And yes, both reactions are still going.

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:21.906
If you said the reverse rate is zero,

00:07:21.987 --> 00:07:24.146
check what is in this flask: there is

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:26.226
no P C L five, so the forward

00:07:26.307 --> 00:07:27.586
rate is zero.

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:30.786
If you said forward falls and reverse rises,

00:07:30.867 --> 00:07:33.186
check which side is full: the rate with

00:07:33.267 --> 00:07:35.426
more to work on starts high.

00:07:35.507 --> 00:07:37.986
If you said the reaction stops, remember the

00:07:38.107 --> 00:07:41.506
concentrations stop changing, but the rates stay equal

00:07:41.547 --> 00:07:42.626
and above zero.

00:07:43.834 --> 00:07:46.553
So whenever a question asks how a reaction

00:07:46.634 --> 00:07:49.833
reaches equilibrium, tell the story in order.

00:07:50.394 --> 00:07:53.433
Start from one side only: that side's rate

00:07:53.514 --> 00:07:55.433
is at its highest and the other rate

00:07:55.594 --> 00:07:56.233
is zero.

00:07:56.874 --> 00:07:58.953
As that side is used up, its rate

00:07:59.034 --> 00:07:59.593
falls.

00:08:00.074 --> 00:08:02.233
As the other side builds up, its rate

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:02.953
rises.

00:08:03.594 --> 00:08:06.233
When the two rates are equal, the concentrations

00:08:06.394 --> 00:08:09.313
stop changing, but neither rate is zero.

00:08:09.754 --> 00:08:12.153
Next, we'll take a flask that is already

00:08:12.194 --> 00:08:14.553
at equilibrium and disturb it, to see what

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:15.513
it does about it.

00:08:16.734 --> 00:08:18.173
Here are the key notes.

00:08:18.414 --> 00:08:20.333
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:20.414 --> 00:08:21.133
to copy them.
